Changes in this branch:

* Add a time axis to the output files, if appropriate.
  - all output in umwmout*-files during a time segment between two restarts is collected in one file
    instead of a sequence of files. An unlimited time axis is added that makes the results readable for many 
    netcdf-based analysis tools like ferret, grads, panoply, ncl ... Not all are tested. 
  - The time stamp in the file name points to the start time of the time slice in the file.
  - Spectral output is already accumulated in single files. The missing time axis is added.
  - calculate times in seconds with respect to some reference time. default: 1970-01-01 00:00
    The reference time may be changed in main.nml 
  - Initialising the model, the initial time step is stored in the output. This information was 
    written in code in the master branch, but is overwritten in the next time step. 
  - Starting from a restart file, the initial (first) time step is not written to output, since it is 
    already stored in the previous output file. This makes aggregation over the time axis of several 
    time slices easier, which would fail, if a time step is found twice.    
    
* ferret does not honor the "description" of a variable. Adding "long_name" makes the output more readable.     
    
* Correct an error in the time span calculated by in datetime_module. The first day has day number 0. 
  Using the new reference time makes the error unvisible, since only differences are used. It is
  corrected anyway.  
